  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An upper level ridge will continue to \nbuild over our area, bringing with it mostly sunny skies, drier \nconditions, and warming temperatures. By Friday afternoon, high \ntemperatures throughout Northern and Central Nevada will be around \nfive degrees above normal for this time of year. Maximum \ntemperatures across Northern and Central Nevada will remain above \nseasonal values this weekend. \n\nLooking ahead to next week, a polar jet will be making its way to \nour region, bringing with it the chance for winter weather and \ncolder temperatures. A cold front associated with an upper level \ntrough will reduce our highs back to the 40s and 50s, as well as \nbring with it the chances for precipitation Tuesday and Wednesday. A \ncolder air mass will also bring our lows down into the 20s and 30s \nnext week. While these lows bring us the slightest bit of hope at \nbuilding the first snowman of the season, confidence in the timing \nand intensity of this forecast is still low. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in the forecast \nfor the remainder of the week. Moderate confidence in the forecast \nfor cooling temperatures early next week. Low confidence remains \nregarding the timing and intensity of the front and its associated \nprecipitation chances early next week. No deviations from the NBM \nmodel output.",
